{
  "_comment": "AUTHORITATIVE shared fixtures for WALLET NFT SUPPORT (docs/WALLET-NFT.md §5). IDENTICAL across blockle-extension/nft.js (JS, reference — authored these), blockle-app/lib (Dart), python/blockle (Python). READ-ONLY inventory + the explicit approved send (calldata only — routes through security.inspectTransaction + the existing signer; the NFT module NEVER signs). Counts/ids/amounts are BigInt-exact base-unit strings. Metadata is NEVER fabricated: an unresolved item keeps what's known with metadataOk:false + metadataNote 'metadata-unavailable'. ipfs:// URIs normalize to config.ipfsGateway; the core fetches NOTHING (the UI loads media). Spam is a conservative FLAG only, never a safety/value claim. The inventory indexer is injected: `raw` maps '<chain>:<ownerAddress>' -> the raw item list getNFTsForOwner returns; an absent/failing indexer adds to `unavailable` (never a fake empty inventory).",
